ile to set permissions.\n\nI need to make sure each task has the correct module calls and parameters. Also, variables like \'docker_compose_url\', \'docker_compose_path\', and \'docker_compose_version\' should be handled properly. The \'v\' removal for comparison is crucial, so I\'ll use replace \'{{ docker_compose_current_version }}\' | replace(\'/v/\', \'\') in the when conditions.\n\nI should structure each task with the appropriate module, arguments, and conditions. Ensuring that each task only runs when necessary, especially the install task which depends on the version comparison.\n\nFinally, I\'ll compile all these tasks into a YAML playbook, starting with \'---\', followed by the tasks in the specified order. I\'ll double-check the YAML syntax and make sure there are no comments or extra explanations, just the tasks as required.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check current docker-compose version\n  command:\n    cmd: docker-compose version\n  register: docker_compose_vsn\n  check_mode: false\n  changed_when: false\n  failed_when: false\n\n- name: Set docker-compose current version fact\n  set_fact:\n    docker_compose_current_version: "{{ docker_compose_vsn.stdout | regex_replace(\'.+(v)(\\\\d+.\\\\d+.\\\\d+)(.*)\', \'\\\\\\\\2\') | trim }}"\n  when: docker_compose_vsn.stdout is defined and docker_compose_vsn.stdout is not empty\n\n- name: Delete existing docker-compose version if it\'s different\n  file:\n    path: "{{ docker_compose_path }}"\n    state: absent\n  when: docker_compose_current_version is not defined or (docker_compose_current_version | replace(\'/v/\', \'\') != docker_compose_version | replace(\'/v/\', \'\'))\n\n- name: Install Docker Compose (if configured)\n  block:\n    - name: Download Docker Compose binary\n      get_url:\n        url: "{{ docker_compose_url }}"\n        dest: "{{ docker_compose_path }}"\n        mode: \'0755\'\n  when: docker_compose_current_version is not defined or docker_compose_current_version is empty or (dock