o ensure each task has the correct module, parameters, and variables. Also, the order of tasks is crucial, so I\'ll arrange them as specified: check existence, check version, download if needed, then copy.\n\nI\'ll structure each task with the appropriate YAML syntax, using \'name\' for the task name, \'action\' for the module, and \'args\' if necessary. I\'ll make sure to use the variables correctly and set conditions where required.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the entire playbook to ensure there are no typos or syntax errors and that it adheres strictly to the user\'s instructions without adding or omitting any tasks.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if the Helm binary exists\n  action: shell stat {{ helm_bin_path }}\n  register: helm_check\n  changed_when: false\n  failed_when: false\n\n- name: Check Helm version\n  action: command helm version --output=json\n  register: helm_existing_version\n  changed_when: false\n  failed_when: false\n\n- name: Download helm\n  action: unarchive\n    remote_src: true\n    url: "{{ helm_download_url }}"\n    dest: "/tmp"\n    archive_file: "{{ helm_repo_path }}-{{ helm_version }}-{{ helm_platform }}-{{ helm_arch }}"\n  register: helm_download\n  when: helm_check.stat.exists == false or helm_existing_version is not defined\n\n- name: Copy helm binary into place\n  action: copy\n    src: "/tmp/./{{ helm_platform }}-{{ helm_arch }}"\n    dest: "{{ helm_bin_path }}"\n    mode: 0755\n  args: { become: true }\n  when: helm_download is changed\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-06T12:24:28.791749609Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 13819385891, 'load_duration': 98275178, 'prompt_eval_count': 592, 'prompt_eval_duration': 286246338, 'eval_count': 785, 'eval_duration': 13433425298, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--e4dc013b-52ff-4e79-8465-baa1fa6f8b63-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 592, 'output_tokens': 785, 'total_tokens': 1377}
