ables and facts. The first task registers bootstrap_facts, which is used in the next tasks. The second task uses the registered output and loops through the map. The third task uses the same map to set the os family.\n\nI need to make sure the tasks are ordered correctly and that the conditions are applied where necessary. Also, the YAML syntax must be correct, with proper indentation and no trailing spaces.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll start with \'---\', then a tasks list, each task as a YAML block with the appropriate module and arguments. I\'ll ensure that each task is correctly structured and that variables are referenced properly.\n\nI think that covers all the requirements. Now, I\'ll structure the playbook accordingly.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: gather_facts | Lookup bootstrap facts\n  raw:\n    cmd: cat /etc/os-release\n  register: bootstrap_facts\n\n- name: gather_facts | Set bootstrap facts (I)\n  set_fact:\n    bootstrap_distribution: "{{ item.value }}"\n    bootstrap_distribution_major_version: "{{ (bootstrap_facts.stdout | regex_search(\'PRETTY_NAME=".*? (\\\\d+).*\') | first) | int }}"\n  loop: "{{ bootstrap_os_family_map.items() }}"\n  when:\n    - bootstrap_facts.rc == 0\n    - not (bootstrap_distribution is defined)\n    - ("{{ item.value }}" in bootstrap_facts.stdout)\n  vars:\n    bootstrap_search: "{{ item.value }}"\n  with_items: "{{ bootstrap_os_family_map.items() }}"\n\n- name: gather_facts | Set bootstrap facts (II)\n  set_fact:\n    bootstrap_os_family: "{{ item.key }}"\n  loop: "{{ bootstrap_os_family_map.items() }}"\n  when: bootstrap_distribution is in item.value\n  loop_control:\n    label: "{{ item.key }}"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-06T12:28:50.337260891Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 18247707585, 'load_duration': 92285194, 'prompt_eval_count': 516, 'prompt_eval_duration': 136110655, 'eval_count': 779, 'eval_duration': 18018403402, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--c0e39662-76d2-4087-9ab3-8450c0c74dc2-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 516, 'output_tokens': 779, 'total_tokens': 1295}
