content='<think>\nAlright, I\'m faced with a problem where an Ansible Playbook didn\'t pass ansible-lint. My task is to fix the playbook while strictly adhering to the original instructions. Let me break down what I need to do.\n\nFirst, I\'ll look at the error messages from ansible-lint to understand what\'s wrong. The errors mention two main issues: \n\n1. "no-changed-when": This rule suggests that commands shouldn\'t change things if nothing needs doing. In Ansible, if a command doesn\'t check for changes, it might run unnecessarily. The example uses `command: echo "File exists!"` without a `changed_when` or `state` check, which is problematic.\n\n2. "fqcn": This stands for Fully Qualified Common Name. Ansible prefers using FQCNs for modules to avoid confusion. The `command` module should be referenced as `ansible.builtin.command` instead of just `command`.\n\nLooking at the faulty playbook, I see that the tasks are using `command` without specifying FQCN. Also, some tasks might not have proper checks for existing files, leading to unnecessary executions.\n\nTo fix this, I\'ll go through each task and make sure they use the correct module names and include appropriate checks for existing files to prevent unnecessary changes.\n\nI\'ll start by replacing `command` with `ansible.builtin.command` wherever necessary. Then, for each task that runs a command only if a file doesn\'t exist, I\'ll add `when` conditions using `file.exists` fact to skip execution if the file is already present.\n\nI\'ll ensure that the task names remain the same and that the order is preserved as per the original instructions. I\'ll also check for any other potential linting issues, like missing `with_items` or incorrect variable references, but based on the errors, the primary fixes are the FQCN and `when` conditions.\n\nAfter making these changes, I\'ll re-run ansible-lint to ensure all issues are resolved. This should result in a valid playbook that meets all the requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Ensure the easy-rsa directory exists\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: Initialize the easy-rsa PKI\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: easyrsa init-pki\n    chdir: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki)\n\n- name: Build the Certificate Authority (CA)\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: EASYRSA_BATCH=yes easyrsa build-ca nopass\n    chdir: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/ca.crt)\n\n- name: Generate Diffie-Hellman parameters\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: easyrsa gen-dh\n    chdir: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/dh.pem)\n\n- name: Build the server certificate\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: EASYRSA_BATCH=yes easyrsa build-server-full server nopass\n    chdir: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/issued/server.crt)\n\n- name: Build the client certificate\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: EASYRSA_BATCH=yes easyrsa build-client-full client nopass\n    chdir: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/issued/client.crt)\n\n- name: Generate the Certificate Revocation List (CRL)\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: easyrsa gen-crl\n    chdir: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/crl.pem)\n\n- name: Generate TLS authentication key\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: openvpn --genkey --secret /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/ta.key\n  when: not file.exists(/etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/ta.key)\n\n- name: Copy PKI files to the server configuration directory\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/{ca.crt,dh.pem,ta.key,client*.crt,server*.crt,ca.key,client*.key,server*.key}\n    dest: /etc/openvpn/server\n    mode: 0640\n    remote_src: yes\n\n- name: Copy ca.crt and ta.key to /etc/openvpn\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki/{ca.crt,ta.key}\n    dest: /etc/openvpn\n    mode: 0640\n    remote_src: yes\n\n- name: Place the server configuration file\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: "{{ openvpn_configuration_directory }}/server.conf.j2"\n    dest: /etc/openvpn/server.conf\n    mode: 0640\n    owner: openvpn\n    group: openvpn\n  notify: Restart openvpn\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-06T12:48:04.263700403Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 25727459615, 'load_duration': 82308462, 'prompt_eval_count': 1820, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1285701083, 'eval_count': 1116, 'eval_duration': 24358330678, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--3b6b1ea8-fd3f-4fe8-b8bf-611f5645cc87-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1820, 'output_tokens': 1116, 'total_tokens': 2936}
