e final corrected playbook will have task 2 with only the apt module, and the dnf module will be removed to fix the YAML syntax error.\n</think>\n\nThe issue was in the second task where both `apt` and `dnf` were incorrectly placed under the same task without proper structure. The corrected playbook removes the `dnf` block to fix the YAML syntax.\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n\n- name: Task 2: Install python pip\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ python_pip_packages }}"\n    state: present\n\n- name: Task 3: Configure pip proxy\n  template:\n    src: pip.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  when: python_pip_proxy is defined\n\n- name: Task 4: Configure trusted hosts\n  template:\n    src: pip.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/pip.conf\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0644\n  when: python_pip_trusted_host is defined\n\n- name: Task 5: Update pip\n  pip:\n    name: "{{ python_pip_pip_package }}"\n    state: "{{ python_pip_pip_state }}"\n    executable: "{{ python_pip_executable }}"\n  when: not (ansible_distribution_version | version_compare(\'=\', \'bookworm\') or\n            ansible_distribution_version | version_compare(\'=\', \'noble\') or\n            ansible_distribution == \'Alpine\')\n\n- name: Task 6: Install requested modules\n  pip:\n    name: "{{ item.name }}"\n    version: "{{ item.version | default(\'latest\') }}"\n    state: "{{ item.state | default(\'present\') }}"\n    executable: "{{ python_pip_executable }}"\n    loop: "{{ python_pip_modules }}"\n  when: not (ansible_distribution_version | version_compare(\'=\', \'bookworm\') or\n            ansible_distribution_version | version_compare(\'=\', \'noble\') or\n            ansible_distribution == \'Alpine\')\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-06T13:14:11.842383299Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 49537233467, 'load_duration': 8