content="<think>\nOkay, I need to fix the Ansible Playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the errors reported.\n\nThe main issue is that the playbook isn't using the fully qualified class names (FQCN) for certain modules. Ansible-lint is flagging modules like set_fact, package, apt_repository, etc., because they're not prefixed with their respective namespaces.\n\nLooking at the tasks:\n\n1. The first two tasks use `set_fact` without the `ansible.builtin.` prefix. I'll change them to `ansible.builtin.set_fact`.\n\n2. The next four tasks include setup files for different OSes. Each of these setup files probably uses modules that aren't using FQCN. For example, setup-RedHat.yml uses `package`, which should be `ansible.builtin.package`.\n\n3. The last task uses `pip`, which should be `ansible.builtin.pip`.\n\nI'll go through each task and update the module names accordingly. Also, I'll ensure that the include_tasks directives point to the correct files without changing their names.\n\nI need to make sure that all module names are updated to their FQCN versions. This should resolve the linting errors without altering the tasks' functionality or order.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Set a fact based on installation method\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    ansible_package_state: present\n  when: ansible_install_method == 'package'\n\n- name: Set a fact based on installation method\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    ansible_package_state: absent\n  when: ansible_install_method != 'package'\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on RedHat\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-RedHat.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_os_family == 'RedHat'\n    - ansible_distribution != 'Fedora'\n    - ansible_install_method == 'package'\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Fedora\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-Fedora.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution == 'Fedora'\n    - ansible_install_method == 'package'\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Ubuntu\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-Ubuntu.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution == 'Ubuntu'\n    - ansible_install_method == 'package'\n\n- name: Set up Ansible on Debian\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-Debian.yml\n  when:\n    - ansible_distribution == 'Debian'\n    - ansible_install_method == 'package'\n\n- name: Set up Ansible using Pip\n  ansible.builtin.include_tasks: setup-pip.yml\n  when: ansible_install_method == 'pip'\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-06T15:21:33.154525505Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11686494318, 'load_duration': 73380459, 'prompt_eval_count': 2711, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1561627363, 'eval_count': 552, 'eval_duration': 10050627559, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--2bac3f5e-1074-42c7-b07a-254d5994bca6-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2711, 'output_tokens': 552, 'total_tokens': 3263}
